// Title: Exchange PowerShell Cmdlet History Deleted
// Sigma ID: a55349d8-9588-4c5a-8e3b-1925fe2a4ffe
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-10-26 | Modified: 2026-10-13
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1070
// Description: Detects the deletion of the Exchange PowerShell cmdlet History logs which may indicate an
//   attempt to destroy forensic evidence
// False positives:
//   - Possible FP during log rotation
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20221012062917/https://m365internals.com/2022/10/07/hunting-in-on-premises-exchange-server-logs/
//   - https://www.it-server-room.com/en/exchange-server-log-file-locations-and-cleanup-guide/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/file/file_delete/file_delete_win_delete_exchange_powershell_logs.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where ActionType =~ "FileDeleted" and (FolderPath contains "\\Logging\\CmdletInfra\\LocalPowerShell\\Cmdlet\\" and FolderPath contains "_Cmdlet_")
